{"articles":{"Adichunchanagiri Hills":{"x":"Adichunchanagiri Hills, is a tourist place near Nagamangala town in Mandya (district), Karnataka State, India.","sights":[{"n":"Soumy Keshava Temple","k":"see","img":"Gopura (main tower) of Saumyakeshava temple at Nagamangala.jpg","ll":[12.81944,76.75361]},{"n":"Driving through the villages","k":"do","d":"It is a pleasant drive from Nagamangala to Adichunchanagiri Hills. Small villages like Tolali,Anchebuhalli and Doodajilla are on the way."},{"n":"Cauvery Sai Dharma","k":"do","d":"Riverside temple"}],"c":[14,30,2,16,33,5,19,35,19,22,35,62,21,32,118,19,29,92,19,28,117,19,27,122,18,27,150,18,27,135,16,27,50,14,27,11],"cs":"est"},"Ambika Kalna":{"x":"Ambika Kalna, or simply Kalna, is a town in the Purba Bardhaman district of West Bengal, India. Situated on the western bank of the Bhagirathi River, it is also called the Temple City for the number of old temples found here. The town got its name from the deity Ma Ambika (incarnation of Goddess Kali) of Siddheswari Temple.","sights":[{"n":"Nava Kailash","k":"see","d":"The temple complex of Nava Kailash consists of 108 Shiva Temples built in aat - chala style. The temple are arranged in two concentric circles.","img":"108 Shiv mandir.jpg","ll":[23.22041,88.36477]},{"n":"Jalesvar Temple","k":"see","d":"The Nava Kailash complex is flanked on either side by two pancha ratna (five-pinnacled) temples. The Jalesvar Temple lies on the west.","img":"Jaleswar Temple, Kalna.jpg","ll":[23.2206,88.36432]},{"n":"Ratneshwar Temple","k":"see","d":"The Nava Kailash complex is flanked on either side by two pancha ratna (five-pinnacled) temples. The Ratneshwar Temple lies on the east.","img":"Ratneswar Temple at Kalna.jpg","ll":[23.22046,88.36534]},{"n":"Pratapeswar Temple","k":"see","d":"Kalna is known for its terracotta temples and the Pratapeswar Temple definitely stands out among the numerous temples of Kalna.","img":"Pratapeswar Shiva Temple.jpg","ll":[23.22103,88.36488]},{"n":"Lalji Mandir","k":"see","d":"Built in 1739, the Lalji Temple is the oldest temple in the Rajbari Complex. It was built by Braja Kishori Devi, the wife of Maharaja Jagat Ram.","img":"Lalji Temple - Kalna (front view) - 2.jpg","ll":[23.22194,88.36523]},{"n":"Brindaban Chandra's Math","k":"see","d":"Temple complex in Guptipara","img":"Brindaban Chandra's Math Complex.jpg","ll":[23.19713,88.44095],"q":"Q56172450"},{"n":"Rupeshwar Shiva Mondir","k":"see","d":"Rupeshwar Shiva Mondir, a flat roof structure with a triple arched entrance. The temple had beautiful stucco work most of it no longer exist.","img":"Rupeswar Temple - Kalna (front view) - 2.jpg","ll":[23.22143,88.36532]},{"n":"Pancharatna Temple","k":"see","d":"A collection of five hat - chala temples standing on a single raised platform. The temples are not identical. They not only differ in size but also in proportion.","img":"Pancha Ratna Temple, Kalna.jpg","ll":[23.22126,88.36536]}],"c":[10,24,11,14,29,18,19,35,29,24,39,50,26,38,144,27,34,221,26,32,316,26,31,282,25,30,232,22,30,130,16,27,17,11,24,9],"cs":"est"},"Anand":{"x":"Anand is a medium-sized city in Central Gujarat, popularly known as the \"milk capital of India.\"","sights":[{"n":"Shri Swaminarayan Mandir, Vadtal","k":"see","d":"Hindu temple in Gujarat, India","img":"Vadtaltemple.jpg","ll":[22.59139,72.87389],"q":"Q7503911"},{"n":"Amul Dairy","k":"see","d":"Asia's largest dairy."},{"n":"Watch a film","k":"do","d":"There are many cinemas in the city."}],"c":[12,29,1,15,33,2,19,38,4,24,42,3,27,43,4,28,38,143,26,32,331,24,31,306,24,31,152,21,33,15,16,32,4,13,30,2],"cs":"est"},"Bakreshwar":{"x":"Bakreshwar is a pilgrimage centre in the central region of West Bengal.","sights":[{"n":"Pahareshwar Kali temple","k":"see","d":"Kali temple in Dubrajpur","img":"Mama Bhagne 1.jpg","ll":[23.78556,87.37056],"q":"Q18987940"},{"n":"Bakreswar Hot Spring","k":"see","d":"There is a warm water pool for bathing.","ll":[23.8814,87.3751]}],"c":[9,24,10,13,29,11,18,35,22,23,39,50,26,39,124,27,35,201,26,32,294,25,31,249,25,30,224,21,29,106,15,27,8,10,24,6],"cs":"est"},"Bandel":{"x":"Bandel is a former Portuguese colony at the Hooghly River, in the Hooghly district of West Bengal.","sights":[{"n":"Bandel Church","k":"see","d":"One of the oldest churches in West Bengal, standing as a memorial to the Portuguese settlement in Bengal. It is dedicated to Our Lady of the Rosary.","img":"Bandel Basilica, Hooghly (West-Bengal).jpg","ll":[22.91895,88.39519]},{"n":"Debanandapur","k":"see","d":"The birthplace of Bengali novelist Sarat Chandra Chattopadhyay (1874–1938).","img":"Debanandapur village in Hooghly district 02.jpg","ll":[22.93778,88.36976]},{"n":"Lahiri Baba Ashram","k":"see","d":"The temple is known for its architecture and environment, and was built in 2003 on the philosophy of Yogiraj Shyamacharan Lahiri.","img":"Lahiri temple Rajhat, Bandel 5.jpg","ll":[22.94091,88.35346]},{"n":"Sayed Jamaluddin Mosque","k":"see","d":"A medieval mosque in Saptagram, built in 1529, and it happens to be the only medieval remains of the flourishing port.","img":"Mosque at Adi Saptagram- 05769.jpg","ll":[22.96042,88.3698]},{"n":"Hangseshwari Temple","k":"see","d":"Temple in Bansberia","img":"Haneswari and Vasudev temples3.jpg","ll":[22.96432,88.39981],"q":"Q5648088"},{"n":"Armenian Church of St. John the Baptist","k":"see","d":"Building in India","img":"Armenian Church, Chinsurah, Hooghly.jpg","ll":[22.8915,88.40126],"q":"Q4505042"},{"n":"Ananta Basudeba Temple","k":"see","d":"Temple in Bansberia","img":"Ananta Basudeba Temple1.JPG","ll":[22.96432,88.39981],"q":"Q4751442"},{"n":"Jubilee Bridge","k":"see","d":"Bridge in India","img":"Jubilee Bridge (Naihati-Bandel) by Piyal Kundu.jpg","ll":[22.90711,88.40444],"q":"Q6301813"}],"c":[10,24,11,14,29,18,19,35,29,24,39,50,26,38,144,27,34,221,26,32,316,26,31,282,25,30,232,22,30,130,16,27,17,11,24,9],"cs":"est"},"Bhedaghat":{"x":"Bhedaghat is a city in the Narmada Valley of Madhya Pradesh, India.","sights":[{"n":"Chausath Yogini Temple, Bhedaghat","k":"see","d":"7th to 10th century circular goddess tradition Hindu temple near Jabalpur","img":"Chausath Yogini Temple, Bhedaghat (30164).jpg","ll":[23.1297,79.8013],"q":"Q17883316"},{"n":"Jabalpur Madan Mahal","k":"see","d":"Human settlement in India","img":"Madan mahal.jpg","ll":[23.14832,79.90157],"q":"Q17058399"},{"n":"Chausat Yogini Temple","k":"see","d":"Situated atop a hillock and approached by a long flight of steps, the Chusat Yogini Temple commands a singularly beautiful view of the Narmada flowing through the jagged…"},{"n":"Dhuandhar Falls","k":"see","d":"The Narmada, making its way through the Marble Rocks, narrows down and then plunges in a waterfall known as Dhuandhar or the \"Smoke Cascade\"."},{"n":"Marble Rocks","k":"see","d":"The perpendicular magnesium limestone rocks fringe the crystal clear placid waters of the Narmada providing a fascinating site."},{"n":"Soapstone Artefacts","k":"see","d":"The soapstone revealed by the Narmada provides occupation to families of carvers of gods and goddesses, lingas, crosses, madonnas, ashtrays and trinket boxes."}],"c":[10,27,19,13,31,19,18,36,19,24,41,8,28,43,17,27,38,177,24,31,409,24,29,404,22,30,222,19,29,33,14,28,7,10,26,5],"cs":"est"},"Chengalpattu":{"x":"Chengalpattu (formerly Chingleput), a town on the Palar River in Tamil Nadu, has developed as a tourist spot for many foreign travellers on their way to Mamallapuram, Thirukazhukundram, Vedanthangal Bird Sanctuary and Kanchipuram, Karikili Bird Sanctuary.","sights":[{"n":"Kolavai Lake","k":"see","d":"The lake hosts migratory birds such as the whiskered tern, Indian spot-billed ducks, moorhens, coots, and small waders.","img":"Kolavai Lake, Chengalpattu in Tamilnadu 07.jpg","ll":[12.71041,79.9892]},{"n":"Vedagiriswarar Temple","k":"see","d":"The temple consists of two structures, one at the foot hill and the other on the hill's crest.","img":"Vedhagireeswarar temple with the tank.jpg","ll":[12.6067,80.0625]},{"n":"Vedanthangal Bird Sanctuary","k":"see","d":"A Ramsar site and the oldest water bird sanctuary in India. It was a favourite hunting spot of the local landlords in the early 18th century.","img":"Vedanthangal Lake.JPG","ll":[12.5456,79.8558]},{"n":"Varaha Cave Temple","k":"see","d":"Temple in India","img":"N-TN-C51 Rock cut Varahar Temple.jpg","ll":[12.6167,80.025],"q":"Q7915405"},{"n":"Patalathri Narasimhar Temple","k":"see","d":"Vishnu Temple In Singaperumalkoil","img":"Singaperumalkovil1.JPG","ll":[12.76194,80.00417],"q":"Q7144201"},{"n":"Kachabeswarar temple, Thirukachur","k":"see","d":"Hindu temple in Tamil Nadu, India","img":"Thirukachur3.JPG","ll":[12.77611,79.99722],"q":"Q16312907"},{"n":"Marundeeswarar Temple, Thirukachur","k":"see","d":"Shiva temple in Tamil Nadu, India","img":"Maruntheeswarar Thirukachur3.JPG","ll":[12.7775,79.99139],"q":"Q24949173"}],"c":[21,27,18,22,29,7,24,32,16,26,34,28,27,34,62,27,34,65,26,33,97,26,32,126,25,31,140,25,30,255,24,28,293,22,27,133],"cs":"est"},"Dimapur":{"x":"Dimapur is the largest city of Nagaland, India.","sights":[{"n":"Dimapur Kalibari","k":"see","d":"Hindu Temple in Nagaland, India","img":"Dimapur Kalibari Temple.jpeg","ll":[25.9043,93.7253],"q":"Q5277164"},{"n":"The Kachari Ruins","k":"see","d":"Ruins in Dimapur, Nagaland, India","img":"Dimapur Ruins 8.jpg","ll":[25.90361,93.74028],"q":"Q7743925"},{"n":"Dimapur Jain Temple","k":"see","d":"Jain Temple in Dimapur, Nagaland","img":"Jain Temple Dimapur.png","ll":[25.90589,93.72485],"q":"Q22907819"},{"n":"Dimapur Ao Baptist Church","k":"see","d":"The largest church in Asia.","ll":[25.75552,93.8736]}],"c":[11,24,10,13,27,22,17,32,49,21,34,129,23,34,192,25,34,233,25,33,249,25,33,224,24,32,179,21,30,93,16,27,21,13,24,11],"cs":"est"},"Gaya":{"x":"Gaya is a major pilgrimage city in Bihar for Hindus. It is visited for doing piṇḍ dān (funeral offerings for the benefit of the soul of the deceased) and for visiting Bodh Gaya and Vishnupad temple.","sights":[{"n":"Mahabodhi Temple","k":"see","d":"Buddhist temple in Bodh Gaya, Bihar, India","img":"Mahabodhitemple.jpg","ll":[24.696,84.99136],"q":"Q4513"},{"n":"Sujata Garh","k":"see","d":"Sujata stupa","img":"Sujata Garh.JPG","ll":[24.69791,85.00332],"q":"Q19284999"},{"n":"The Great Buddha","k":"see","d":"Buddha's statue","img":"Bodh Gaya - Buddha Statue - Front View (9224970905).jpg","ll":[24.69047,84.98181],"q":"Q7737678"},{"n":"Chatta Masjid","k":"see","d":"Congregational mosque in Gaya, Bihar, India","img":"Chatta Masjid Gaya.jpg","ll":[24.79556,85.00806],"q":"Q109300179"},{"n":"Archaeological Museum of Bodhgaya","k":"see","d":"Archaeology museum in Bodhgaya, Bihar, India","img":"Ticket Counter - Bodh Gaya ASI Museum.jpg","ll":[24.69472,84.98722],"q":"Q113987917"},{"n":"Brahmayoni","k":"see","d":"Hillock, which offers nice bird's eye view of the plains."}],"c":[8,23,14,12,27,14,16,33,12,22,39,10,26,40,35,27,38,155,26,34,273,26,33,267,25,32,180,21,32,53,14,29,8,10,25,3],"cs":"imd"},"Gurugram":{"x":"Gurugram or Gurgaon, a satellite city in South Haryana, is a major IT and shopping hub of Delhi. Once a mere commuter town, Gurugram now boasts slick office complexes housing companies from Accenture to Xerox, with more shopping malls per square mile than anywhere else in India. However, the city is also one of the victims of Delhi's unprecedented urban sprawl, with poor infrastructure, traffic jams as well as the winter smog.","sights":[{"n":"Damdama Lake","k":"see","img":"Haryana Tourism restaurant on Damdama Lake.JPG","ll":[28.304,77.129]},{"n":"Aravali Biodiversity Park","k":"see","d":"The park on the Aravalli Range includes a number of trails and a native plant nursery and interpretive displays at the entrance.","img":"Aravalli BDPark 2015-01-17-021.jpg","ll":[28.48321,77.11189]},{"n":"Tau Devi Lal Stadium","k":"do","d":"A multi-purpose sports complex hosting football and cricket matches.","img":"Tau Devilal stadium.jpg","ll":[28.44222,77.03639]},{"n":"Sohna Lake","k":"see","d":"Sohna Lake is about 10 km from Gurgaon. It is best to visit after rainfall and during winters."},{"n":"Vintage Camera Museum and Foundation","k":"see","d":"India's largest camera museum. One can visit from Tuesday-Saturday from 11AM-5PM only via appointments."},{"n":"NeverEnuf Garden Railway","k":"see","d":"Miniature railway modelling project about 5 km off National Highway 8 through a bumpy road."}],"c":[6,21,14,9,26,20,15,32,18,22,39,16,27,43,34,30,42,71,28,37,178,26,35,175,23,34,100,18,33,11,13,28,4,8,23,7],"cs":"est"},"Kodikunnu":{"x":"Kodikunnu is in Central Kerala, India.","sights":[{"n":"Kodikkunnu Bhagavathy Temple","k":"see","img":"Kodikkunnu Bhagavathi Temple.jpg","ll":[10.83051,76.11539]},{"n":"Abaya Pradhan Temple","k":"see","d":"Building in India","img":"Thirumittakode Anchumoorthi Temple.jpg","ll":[10.78278,76.18417],"q":"Q4663603"},{"n":"Puramundekkadu Shri Mahadeva Temple","k":"see","d":"Hindu temple in Kerala, India","img":"പുരമുണ്ടേക്കാട്ട് മഹാദേവക്ഷേത്രം.jpg","ll":[10.77916,76.02616],"q":"Q13113359"},{"n":"Panniyur Sri Varahamoorthy Temple","k":"see","d":"Vishnu avatar temple in Kerala, India","img":"Panniyur Varahamoorthy temple, Kumbidi Kerala 20210707.jpg","ll":[10.82686,76.05528],"q":"Q7131411"},{"n":"Kattil Madam Temple, Chalapuram","k":"see","d":"11th century Hindu temple in India","img":"Kattilmadam (Kallilmadam).JPG","ll":[10.77067,76.15333],"q":"Q18126673"},{"n":"Trithala Maha Siva Temple","k":"see","d":"Hindu temple in Kerala, India","img":"തൃത്താലക്ഷേത്രം.jpg","ll":[10.80377,76.13722],"q":"Q13112600"},{"n":"Malamakkavu Ayyappa Temple","k":"see","d":"Hindu temple in Kerala, India","img":"Malamakkavu Temple.jpg","ll":[10.8185,76.079],"q":"Q6741216"},{"n":"Kaithali Temple","k":"see","d":"9th century Hindu temples complex in central Kerala","img":"Kaithali.jpg","ll":[10.80751,76.18952],"q":"Q41135737"}],"c":[21,33,6,22,36,10,24,37,34,25,35,82,26,32,188,25,29,393,24,28,375,24,28,283,24,29,214,24,30,246,23,30,127,21,31,26],"cs":"est"},"Mathura":{"x":"Mathura is a Hindu holy city at the banks of the Yamuna River, in the Braj region of Uttar Pradesh, India. It is a famous pilgrimage city as Krishna was believed to born here as an avatar of the Hindu god Vishnu.","sights":[{"n":"Government Museum","k":"see","d":"Biggest and richest in Asia for Mathura and Gandhar sculpture. It has one of the finest collection of archaeological interest.","img":"Government Museum - Mathura 2013-02-23 5016.JPG","ll":[27.49566,77.67924]},{"n":"Banke Bihari Temple","k":"see","d":"Temple of Radha Krishna in Vrindavan, India","img":"Bankebihari temple main gate Vrindavan.JPG","ll":[27.57976,77.69051],"q":"Q3630572"},{"n":"Krishna Janmasthan Temple Complex","k":"see","d":"Hindu Temple complex in Mathura, India believed as the place of birth of Krishna","img":"Mathura Temple-Mathura-India0002.JPG","ll":[27.50475,77.66975],"q":"Q6394892"},{"n":"Prem Mandir","k":"see","d":"Hindu temple in Vrindavan, Uttar Pradesh, India","img":"PremMandirSideViewFromCanteen.jpg","ll":[27.5725,77.6725],"q":"Q16609019"},{"n":"Vrindavan Chandrodaya Mandir","k":"see","d":"Hindu temple in Vrindavan, India","img":"Vrindavan Chandrodaya Mandir (VCM) Temple.jpg","ll":[27.5725,77.6725],"q":"Q16902821"},{"n":"ISKCON Temple, Vrindavan","k":"see","d":"ISKCON Temple in Vrindavan","img":"Radha Syamasundar Vrindavan Radhastami 2004.jpg","ll":[27.57242,77.67775],"q":"Q4500831"},{"n":"Radha Vallabh Temple","k":"see","d":"Hindu temple in Vindravan, Uttar Pradesh, India","img":"Temple of Radha Ballabh.jpg","ll":[27.58066,77.69156],"q":"Q12449473"},{"n":"Madan Mohan Temple","k":"see","d":"Hindu temple in Vrindavan, Uttar Pradesh, India","img":"MadanMohanmandir.jpg","ll":[27.58009,77.68772],"q":"Q4500833"}],"c":[6,22,12,10,27,14,16,34,12,23,40,11,28,43,22,31,43,63,28,37,177,26,34,171,24,34,88,19,33,17,13,29,4,8,24,6],"cs":"est"},"Nashik":{"x":"Nashik is a city in the state of Maharashtra with a population of about 2.3 million people (2023). This is an ancient holy city, also known as the Wine Capital of India, part of the Mumbai - Pune - Nashik so-called \"golden triangle of Maharashtra\", a city of pilgrimage for many Hindus, important for Hindu rituals for the afterlife offerings, and also famous for the Hindu pilgrimage Kumbh Mela, gathering hundreds of millions of pilgrims every 12 years.","sights":[{"n":"Gangapur Dam","k":"see","img":"Canal tower of Gangapur Dam India.jpg","ll":[20.02606,73.66715]},{"n":"Kalaram Temple","k":"see","d":"An important temple and landmark in Panchavati area.","img":"Kalaram Temple Nashik Corner View.jpg","ll":[20.00691,73.79555]},{"n":"Nashik Caves","k":"see","d":"Buddhist and Jain Caves dating back to 2nd century BCE on Nashik- Mumbai highway near Pathardi phata. They are on top of a hill.","img":"028 Caves 6-9 (33928459836).jpg","ll":[19.94167,73.74861]},{"n":"Shri Tryambakeshwar Jyotirlinga Temple","k":"see","d":"One of the 12 Jyotirlingas in India, and is the most sacred place in Nashik. Nearby is also the Brahma giri, where lord Shiva performed the tandava dance.","img":"Trimbakeshwar nj.jpg","ll":[19.93224,73.53069]},{"n":"Statue of Ahimsa","k":"see","d":"Jain idol","img":"Shri 1008 Rishabdev Bhagwan 108 idol at Mangi Tungi.jpg","ll":[20.0,73.78],"q":"Q22813236"},{"n":"Gajpanth","k":"see","d":"Digambar Jain pilgrimage site in Maharashtra","img":"Dharmachakra, lord mahaviras temple.jpg","ll":[20.06305,73.79246],"q":"Q24939830"}],"c":[10,29,1,13,32,3,16,35,8,20,38,1,22,37,10,23,32,120,22,28,241,22,28,196,21,29,169,19,32,68,15,31,26,12,29,2],"cs":"imd"},"Ramanathapuram":{"x":"Ramanathapuram or Ramnad, a town in southern Tamil Nadu, is the gateway to Rameswaram and Dhanushkodi.","sights":[{"n":"Thiruppullani","k":"see","d":"Temple in India","img":"Tirupullani1.jpg","ll":[9.2885,78.83446],"q":"Q7785436"},{"n":"Ramalinga Vilasam","k":"see","d":"The palace of the Sethupathi family.","ll":[9.37125,78.82739]}],"c":[22,29,16,23,32,16,25,34,26,27,34,58,27,34,85,26,33,40,26,33,47,25,33,62,25,33,91,25,31,208,24,29,224,23,28,96],"cs":"est"},"Ranaghat":{"x":"Ranaghat is a small town along the river Churni in the Nadia district of West Bengal. The name Ranaghat comes from the name of a Dakat Rana. This is the great character of Vande Mataram by Bankim Chandra Chattopadhyay.","sights":[{"n":"Churni River","k":"do","d":"A boat cruise in Churni during moonlight is a treat. The place is ideal for a day picnic."}],"c":[10,25,11,14,30,19,19,36,32,24,39,59,26,37,165,26,33,244,26,31,342,26,31,301,25,30,238,22,30,148,16,27,23,11,25,11],"cs":"est"},"Siliguri":{"x":"Siliguri, the largest city in northern West Bengal, is a liberal and cosmopolitan city that is known for its vibrant music scene and strong youth culture. On the banks of the Mahananda River and the Teesta River at the foothills of the Darjeeling Hills, Siliguri is the third-largest urban agglomeration in West Bengal. It is known as the \"Gateway of North-Eastern India\" as it connects North-Eastern India with the mainland through a narrow strip of land, making it a major trading and transport hub.","sights":[{"n":"Tashi Gomang Shedra Buddhist Monastery","k":"see","d":"Inaugurated by the Dalai Lama in 1999, and belongs to the Kagyu tradition of Tibetan Buddhism.","img":"Tashi Gomang stupa, Salugara 03.jpg","ll":[26.76659,88.44491]},{"n":"Buddha Mundir Monastery","k":"see","d":"A monastery established by the Nyingma yogi, Chatral Sangye Dorji Rinpoche","ll":[26.76622,88.44426]},{"n":"Ewam (Nupchen Namchak) Monastery","k":"see","d":"A large Buddhist monastery in the Nyingma tradition.","ll":[26.8024,88.4336]},{"n":"ISKCON Temple","k":"see","d":"It houses many beautiful idols of Advaita Acharya, Lord Narasimha, Lord Chaitanya and many more.","ll":[26.72913,88.40831]},{"n":"Khordong Byangter Monastery","k":"see","d":"A monastery is in the Nyingma tradition of Tibetan Buddhism. Accommodation available at the compound.","ll":[26.66687,88.36175]},{"n":"Triratna Monastery","k":"see","d":"A monastery in the Nyingma tradition of Tibetan Buddhism","ll":[26.7631,88.4475]}],"c":[11,22,23,13,24,24,16,29,34,20,31,76,22,30,249,24,30,628,25,29,843,25,30,589,24,29,403,20,28,121,15,26,10,12,23,11],"cs":"imd"},"Central Travancore":{"x":"Central Travancore is in Kerala in India.","sights":[{"n":"Sreevallabha Temple, Thiruvalla","k":"see","d":"Pre-11th century Hindu temple in Kerala","img":"Sree Vallaba Temple 5.JPG","ll":[9.37375,76.5626],"q":"Q3595367"},{"n":"Aranmula Parthasarathy Temple","k":"see","d":"Hindu temple of Krishna near Aranmula, India","img":"Aranmula Temple.JPG","ll":[9.32778,76.68833],"q":"Q4784133"},{"n":"Kaviyoor Mahadeva Temple, Kerala","k":"see","d":"10th century Hindu temple","img":"009242022 Kaviyur Mahadeva Temple Kerala 108.jpg","ll":[9.39639,76.61056],"q":"Q6379319"},{"n":"Puliyur Mahavishnu Temple","k":"see","d":"Building in India","img":"Thripuliyoor Mahavishnu1.JPG","ll":[9.30194,76.58583],"q":"Q7259367"},{"n":"Thrichittatt Maha Vishnu Temple","k":"see","d":"Building in India","img":"Thrichittatt Maha Vishnu Temple1.JPG","ll":[9.32667,76.6042],"q":"Q7798125"},{"n":"Thiruvanvandoor Mahavishnu Temple","k":"see","d":"Building in India","img":"Thiruvanvandoor Pambanaiappan Temple 1.JPG","ll":[9.34306,76.5797],"q":"Q7785522"},{"n":"Thiruvatta Mahadeva Temple","k":"see","d":"Hindu temple in Kerala, India","img":"Thiruvatta Sivan (4).JPG","ll":[9.37074,76.57086],"q":"Q13112517"},{"n":"St. John's Cathedral, Tiruvalla","k":"see","d":"Building in India","img":"St. John's Cathedral, Tiruvalla.jpg","ll":[9.37906,76.57019],"q":"Q17021206"}],"c":[20,31,15,21,34,26,23,36,59,25,34,125,25,31,250,25,29,352,24,28,302,24,28,256,24,29,252,24,29,348,23,29,198,21,29,46],"cs":"est"},"Tiruvannamalai":{"x":"Tiruvannamalai, also known as Arunachala, is one of the greatest Saivite shrines in Tamil Nadu, India, on a sprawling 24 acre temple campus, drawing hundreds of thousands of pilgrims every full moon. The hill here is considered to be a manifestation of Shiva. Tiruvannamalai is one of the Panchabhoota Stalams signifying the 